IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc19-s492-27-to-3`

-- ccc19-tests-s492-27-to-3.l4 -- tests for ccc19-s492-27-to-3.l4 (Criminal Code (Canada) ss 492.27 to 492.3, Days to Be Excluded).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the run. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- Date arithmetic checked by hand: a hearing on 1 June 2026; 2 April 2026 is exactly 60 days before it (at least 60: in time), 3 April is 59 days before (late), 1 April is 61 days before (in time).
-- Argument order of the limb functions: the court is determining; the answer of s 492.3; the filing (or service) date; the clerk seam (limbs (a), (c)); the hearing date; the kind of day.

§ `s 492.27 -- the chapeau: Subject to section 492.3, in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall not take into account any day within any of the following periods`

-- not determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay: the text's "in determining" is not met
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- determining, the limb's period does not cover the day: the text says no ("any day within")
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- determining, the day is within the period, s 492.3 does not apply (JUST FALSE or NOTHING from it): barred
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- determining, the day is within the period, but s 492.3 applies: "Subject to section 492.3", the text does not say what days remain, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the period itself is not covered: not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: where the limb's answer is JUST TRUE the court SHANT take the day into account (taking it into account is a BREACH); otherwise nothing is owed.
#TRACE `s 492.27 the prohibition on the court taking the day into account` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

#TRACE `s 492.27 the prohibition on the court taking the day into account` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.27 take the day into account in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` AT 4

#TRACE `s 492.27 the prohibition on the court taking the day into account` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

#TRACE `s 492.27 the prohibition on the court taking the day into account` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§ `s 492.27(a) -- an application under section 276.01, if a copy was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in section 276.02`

-- filed exactly 60 days before the hearing, with the clerk: "at least 60 days" is met, so the "if" is not met, whatever the day
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- filed 61 days before: in time
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- filed 59 days before: late. (a)(i) a day it took to hear the application; (a)(ii) a day in another period the court has determined is attributable; a day in neither is not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period` EQUALS NOTHING
-- never filed at all: not filed at least 60 days before the hearing, whoever the clerk is, so the limb applies
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- filed 61 days before, but with a person who is not the clerk of the court (the section 2 seam answers JUST FALSE): not filed with the clerk, so late
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- filed with a person the section 2 definition does not settle (the seam answers NOTHING): not covered, carried through
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- late filing and a day in (a)(i), but s 492.3 applies: not covered; and with an in-time filing s 492.3 does not matter
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the period test on its own, and the helper
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) a copy of the application was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing` (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(a) a copy of the application was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing` (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 492.27(b) -- an application under section 278.12 or 278.21, if a copy was not served at least 60 days before the hearing`

-- served on every one of the persons exactly 60 days before: in time
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 2 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- served 61 days before: in time
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- served 59 days before: late
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not yet served on every one of the persons: not served at least 60 days before
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay; and s 492.3 applying
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.27(b) the court shall not take the day into account` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST (Date 3 4 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` EQUALS NOTHING

