§ `s 492.3 -- the court shall take into account any frivolous or dilatory action, or any action not made in good faith`
-- in relation to an application or objection of ss 492.27 to 492.29; a frivolous, dilatory or bad-faith action; by each of the three named kinds of person: the duty
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 counsel representing the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 a person acting on behalf of the prosecutor or the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- by someone else (the accused's own counsel, say): not named, not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an action that is not frivolous, dilatory or in bad faith: not named, not covered
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` TRUE FALSE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not in relation to an application or objection referred to in ss 492.27 to 492.29: the text's "in relation to" is not met
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` FALSE TRUE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` FALSE FALSE `s 492.3 someone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: a duty on the court that stands until performed (no period); performed, FULFILLED; not owed, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 492.3 the duty of the court to take the action into account` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

#TRACE `s 492.3 the duty of the court to take the action into account` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 492.3 take the action into account in determining the days that are not to be taken into account` AT 6

#TRACE `s 492.3 the duty of the court to take the action into account` TRUE TRUE `s 492.3 someone else` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

#TRACE `s 492.3 the duty of the court to take the action into account` FALSE TRUE `s 492.3 the prosecutor` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)
